   "title": "Russia's FSB Says Minor Detained Over Moscow Park Attack Threat After U.S. Tip-Off",
   "url": "https://www.themoscowtimes.com/2026/11/01/russias-fsb-says-minor-detained-over-moscow-park-attack-threat-after-us-tip-off-a94148",
   "domain": "themoscowtimes.com",
   "source": "themoscowtimes.com",
   "published": "Sun, 01 Nov 2026 17:18:00 +0300",
   "_dt": 1793542680.0,
   "ageDays": 0.28,
   "summary": "Russia's FSB security service said on Sunday that an underage Russian national was detained over a threat to carry out a terrorist attack in Moscow's Tsaritsyno Park, after Russia received a tip-off from the United States, Interfax reported. The U.S. Embassy in Moscow on Saturday issued an urgent security alert warning of a credible threat of a mass casualty event at the museum reserve that day.",
   "summary_zh": "俄罗斯联邦安全局星期日表示，俄罗斯收到美国提供的线索后，拘留了一名涉嫌威胁在莫斯科沙皇村公园实施恐怖袭击的未成年俄罗斯人，据国际文传电讯社报道。美国驻莫斯科大使馆星期六发布紧急安全警报，警告当天博物馆园区存在可信的大规模伤亡事件威胁。",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "Russia's FSB security service said on Sunday that an underage Russian national was detained over a threat to carry out a terrorist attack in Moscow's Tsaritsyno Park, after Russia received a tip-off from the United States, Interfax reported. \"We are grateful to the American side for providing the information,\" the security service was quoted as saying in a statement. The U.S. Embassy in Moscow on Saturday issued an urgent security alert warning of a credible threat of a mass casualty event at the museum reserve that day. The embassy said the U.S. government was coordinating with Russian authorities on a response and urged people to avoid the area and take precautions to ensure their safety. The FSB later confirmed that it had received information from the United States about plans for a terrorist attack in Moscow and was taking action. Tsaritsyno was evacuated Saturday during a concert by musician Lilia Pechenkina. “Just as I was playing the last piece in the program, an evacuation announcement came over the loudspeaker,” Pechenkina told the news outlet Ostorozhno, Novosti. Around 50 law enforcement officers were dispatched to the area, with police vehicles patrolling the perimeter, according to the Baza Telegram channel, which is reported to have ties to Russia’s security services. In 2024, the U.S. warned of an impending terrorist threat in Moscow ahead of the March 22 attack on Crocus City Hall, which killed 145 people and wounded hundreds more. Russian foreign intelligence chief Sergei Naryshkin later said the U.S. information had been “too general” to identify the attackers. We are facing unprecedented challenges. Russia's Prosecutor General's Office has designated The Moscow Times as an \"undesirable\" organization, criminalizing our work and putting our staff at risk of prosecution. This follows our earlier unjust labeling as a \"foreign agent.\" These actions are direct attempts to silence independent journalism in Russia. The authorities claim our work \"discredits the decisions of the Russian leadership.\" We see things differently: we strive to provide accurate, unbiased reporting on Russia. We, the journalists of The Moscow Times, refuse to be silenced. But to continue our work, we need your help . Your support, no matter how small, makes a world of difference. If you can, please support us monthly starting from just $ 2. It's quick to set up, and every contribution makes a significant impact. By supporting The Moscow Times, you're defending open, independent journalism in the face of repression. Thank you for standing with us",
   "bodyLevel": "fulltext",
   "country": [
    "ru"
   ],
   "topic": [
    "sec",
    "pol"
   ],
   "tier": 2,
   "actor": "美国",
   "alsoUS": false,
   "cnHit": false,
   "usHit": true,
   "terrHit": false,
   "riskHit": false,
