   "title": "Ganduje’s Okorocha Visit Exposes APC Cracks",
   "url": "https://leadership.ng/gandujes-okorocha-visit-exposes-apc-cracks/",
   "domain": "leadership.ng",
   "source": "Leadership（尼日利亚）",
   "published": "Sun, 01 Nov 2026 08:40:38 +0000",
   "_dt": 1793522438.0,
   "ageDays": 0.51,
   "summary": "While the Imo APC insists Governor Hope Uzodimma remains its candidate and vows to challenge the ruling, Ganduje, a former national chairman, has publicly described Okorocha’s victory as deserved. Could Ganduje’s gesture indirectly strengthen forces challenging the governor, including those associated with Nyesom Wike, who has vowed to prevent Uzodimma from becoming Senate President? The episode exposes competing interests within the APC.",
   "summary_zh": "尽管伊莫州全进步大会党坚持州长希望·乌佐迪马仍是该党候选人，并誓言挑战现任州长甘杜耶，但这位前全国主席公开称奥科罗查赢得选举是理所应当的。甘杜耶的这一举动是否可能间接增强挑战州长的力量，包括与曾誓言阻止乌佐迪马成为参议院议长的尼耶松·维耶有关联的力量？这一事件暴露了全进步大会党内部相互 competing 的利益。",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "While the Imo APC insists Governor Hope Uzodimma remains its candidate and vows to challenge the ruling, Ganduje, a former national chairman, has publicly described Okorocha’s victory as deserved. Is this simply personal solidarity, or a signal of deeper political realignments within the ruling party? The speculation becomes more intriguing given Uzodimma’s strategic importance within President Bola Tinubu’s political machinery. Could Ganduje’s gesture indirectly strengthen forces challenging the governor, including those associated with Nyesom Wike, who has vowed to prevent Uzodimma from becoming Senate President? The episode exposes competing interests within the APC. The bigger question is whether the party can reconcile these divisions before internal disputes become electoral liabilities. We’ve got the edge. Get real-time reports, breaking scoops, and exclusive angles delivered straight to your phone. Don’t settle for stale news. Join LEADERSHIP NEWS on WhatsApp for 24/7 updates →",
