   "title": "How Yerima, Yari and Matawalle Underdeveloped Zamfara",
   "url": "https://www.thisdaylive.com/2026/11/01/how-yerima-yari-and-matawalle-underdeveloped-zamfara/",
   "domain": "thisdaylive.com",
   "source": "ThisDay（尼日利亚）",
   "published": "Sun, 01 Nov 2026 02:26:50 +0000",
   "_dt": 1793500010.0,
   "ageDays": 0.77,
   "summary": "For instance, Maradun is the home of the Minister of State for Defence, Bello Matawalle, who is also the immediate past governor of Zamfara State. Zamfara is also the home of Senator Abdulaziz Yari, the Director-General of the All Progressives Congress (APC) Presidential Campaign Council mandated to oversee the re-election campaign of President Bola Tinubu. Both communities are in the same Zamfara West Senatorial District currently represented in the Senate by Senate Yari, who was also governor of the state.",
   "summary_zh": "例如，马拉敦是国防部国务部长贝洛·马塔瓦莱的家乡，他也是赞法拉州最近一任州长。参议员阿卜杜勒阿齐兹·亚里来自赞法拉州，他担任全进步大会党（APC）总统竞选委员会主任，负责监督总统博拉·蒂努布的连任竞选。这两个地区都位于赞法拉州西部参议员选区，该选区目前由参议员亚里在参议院代表，他此前也曾担任该州州长。",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "The Zamfara State Police Command recently announced the arrest of a 22-year-old member of the Jama’atu Izalatil Bid’ah Wa’iqamatus Sunnah (JIBWIS), Umar Ibrahim Gandi Maradun for chanting incitements to religious violence in Nigeria. In a viral video, the accused was seen leading the chant: “Give Us Rifles to Kill Arna (infidels/Christians)….” in places like Enugu and Jos. According to the police, the suspect was located in Maradun. However, the police said the road from Gusau to Maradun was so bad that they had to contact JIBWIS in Maradun to bring the suspect to Gusau, in a motorcycle, popularly known as Okada. The matter became more disturbing considering the fact that the three former governors of the state since the enthronement of democracy almost came from nearly the affected area. For instance, Maradun is the home of the Minister of State for Defence, Bello Matawalle, who is also the immediate past governor of Zamfara State. The distance from Gusau to Maradun is officially between 91 to 100 kilometres. That should ordinarily take about 70 minutes on a modestly bad road. Now it takes over 180 minutes due mostly to the unmotorable nature of the road, and worsened by insecurity. Zamfara is also the home of Senator Abdulaziz Yari, the Director-General of the All Progressives Congress (APC) Presidential Campaign Council mandated to oversee the re-election campaign of President Bola Tinubu. He is from Talata Mafara, which is separated from Maradun by less than 25 kilometres. Both communities are in the same Zamfara West Senatorial District currently represented in the Senate by Senate Yari, who was also governor of the state. According to media reports, the bad road continues to the village of Senator Yari, through to Talata Mafara Central Primary School where he graduated. Also from Zamfara West is Senator Sani Yerima, who comes from Anka, about 110 kilometres from Gusau. He was also Governor of the state for eight years until 2007 and senator thereafter for 12 years from 2007-2019. Reports claim there is also no road to his place. The state also witnessed the worst form of insecurity when the three were governors. These are the three men leading the charge to bring Renewed Hope to Nigerians. Charity, they say, begins at home. To many, the trio failed the people of the state. Founded on January 22, 1995, THISDAY is published by THISDAY NEWSPAPERS LTD., 35 Creek Road Apapa, Lagos, Nigeria with offices in 36 states of Nigeria , the Federal Capital Territory and around the world. It is Nigeria’s most authoritative news media available on all platforms for the political, business, professional and diplomatic elite and broader middle classes while serving as the meeting point of new ideas, culture and technology for the aspirationals and millennials. The newspaper is a public trust dedicated to the pursuit of truth and reason covering a range of issues from breaking news to politics, business, the markets, the arts, sports and community to the crossroads of people and society. You can email us at: hello@thisdaylive.com or visit our contact us page",
   "bodyLevel": "fulltext",
