   "title": "IOC says crude Q2 price volatile as procurement swings between discounts and premiums",
   "url": "https://www.thehindu.com/business/Economy/crude-oil-prices-very-volatile-in-q2-carried-both-discounts-premium-at-varying-intervals-iocl-official/article71650317.ece",
   "domain": "thehindu.com",
   "source": "thehindu.com",
   "published": "Sat, 31 Oct 2026 21:39:42 +0530",
   "_dt": 1793462982.0,
   "ageDays": 1.2,
   "summary": "Unlock these with Subscription Crude oil procurement remained volatile during the September quarter, with Indian Oil Corporation (IOC) sourcing supplies at discounts of up to $5 per barrel and premiums of as much as $12, Anuj Jain, Director (Finance), told investors during a post-results call on Saturday. Explaining the volatility in procurement costs, he said crude purchases during the quarter ranged from a discount of $5 per barrel to a premium of $12 against prevailing benchmark prices.",
   "summary_zh": "订阅即可解锁这些内容。9月季度原油采购价格持续波动。印度石油公司（IOC）财务总监阿努吉·贾因（Anuj Jain）周六在业绩公布后的电话会议上告诉投资者，该公司以每桶最高折价5美元、最高溢价12美元的价格采购原油。他解释采购成本的波动时说，该季度的原油采购价格相对于当时基准价格介于每桶折价5美元和溢价12美元之间。",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "Account subscription benefits alongside Premium Stories, Editorials, Opinions and more. Unlock these with Subscription Crude oil procurement remained volatile during the September quarter, with Indian Oil Corporation (IOC) sourcing supplies at discounts of up to $5 per barrel and premiums of as much as $12, Anuj Jain, Director (Finance), told investors during a post-results call on Saturday. The Delhi-headquartered refiner’s net profit more than doubled year-on-year to ₹21,630 crore in the second quarter, supported by improved refining margins and a brief decline in benchmark crude oil prices. Mr. Jain said LPG under-recoveries stood at ₹184 per cylinder in September before rising to ₹229 in October. These are projected to increase further to ₹309 in November and ₹370 in December. Explaining the volatility in procurement costs, he said crude purchases during the quarter ranged from a discount of $5 per barrel to a premium of $12 against prevailing benchmark prices. In the first quarter, the range was from zero discount or premium to a premium of $18 per barrel. Effective procurement prices depend on several factors, including whether supplies are contracted on a free-on-board (FOB) or delivered-at-place (DAP) basis, freight costs and the grade of crude. Russian crude accounted for around 55% of IOC’s crude basket during the first half of the fiscal, followed by supplies from the Middle East, primarily Saudi Arabia and Dubai, at 24%. Africa, including Angola and Nigeria, contributed about 10%, while Brazil accounted for 7%. Supplies from the U.S. and Venezuela made up the remaining 2-5% and 3-4%, respectively. Around 87% of the company’s crude procurement during the period came through spot sourcing. Mr. Jain said. Responding to a question on whether spot purchases entailed higher costs, he said such sourcing did not necessarily mean paying a premium, as prices varied across region/geography. “Now, within spot you have Russian crude. Sometimes, we are getting a high discount, sometimes we are paying a premium as well,” Mr. Jain said. “In the few months, we have seen huge, discounted crude coming in from Iraq. So, the moment it is available, we are buying huge quantities from Iraq also. That used to be our staple diet before the [West Asia] crisis as well.” He added that procurement economics were also influenced by effective negotiations, which played an important role in determining the final price. Comments have to be in English, and in full sentences. They cannot be abusive or personal. Please abide by our community guidelines for posting your comments. We have migrated to a new commenting platform. If you are already a registered user of The Hindu and logged in, you may continue to engage with our articles. If you do not have an account please register and login to post comments. Users can access their older comments by logging into their accounts on Vuukle",
