   "title": "EU diplomats object to G20 photo with Lavrov, prompting US cancellation",
   "url": "https://www.euronews.com/2026/10/30/eu-diplomats-object-to-g20-photo-with-lavrov-prompting-us-cancellation",
   "domain": "euronews.com",
   "source": "euronews.com",
   "published": "Fri, 30 Oct 2026 18:03:13 +0100",
   "_dt": 1793379793.0,
   "ageDays": 2.16,
   "summary": "The United States cancelled a planned group photo of foreign ministers from the world's 20 largest economies (G20) on Friday after several European diplomats objected to being photographed alongside Russian Foreign Minister Sergey Lavrov and threatened to walk out. US Secretary of State Marco Rubio decided to cancel the photo to avoid further controversy, according to two US officials who spoke on condition of anonymity because of the sensitivity of the matter.",
   "summary_zh": "美国于周五取消了原定的20个全球最大经济体（G20）外长集体合影计划。此前，数名欧洲外交官反对与俄罗斯外长谢尔盖·拉夫罗夫一起拍照，并威胁退出合影。两名美国官员表示，由于此事敏感，他们要求匿名知情；国务卿马可·鲁比奥为避免引发更多争议，决定取消此次拍摄。",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "Share Comments Add Euronews on Google Share Facebook Twitter Flipboard Send Reddit Linkedin Messenger Telegram VK Bluesky Threads Whatsapp The meeting in Atlanta will go ahead as planned, ahead of a G20 leaders’ summit hosted by President Donald Trump at his Miami golf club in December. The United States cancelled a planned group photo of foreign ministers from the world's 20 largest economies (G20) on Friday after several European diplomats objected to being photographed alongside Russian Foreign Minister Sergey Lavrov and threatened to walk out. US Secretary of State Marco Rubio decided to cancel the photo to avoid further controversy, according to two US officials who spoke on condition of anonymity because of the sensitivity of the matter. Opening the talks, Rubio looked ahead, saying he hoped for “a productive meeting.” “We are in a critical moment — I would call it a moment of choosing, and I would say not just for my country, the United States of America, but frankly, for the world,\" he said. The cancellation of the traditional group photo highlighted tensions within the G20, as diplomats face difficult negotiations over the war in Ukraine, the US-Israeli war against Iran, US tariffs and disputes in the South China Sea. German Foreign Minister Johann Wadephul said “there is no normality with Russia” but “we must exchange the controversies at the table here,” the German news agency dpa reported. He added that “we also must not send falsely optimistic signals.” Even before the dispute over the photo, several G20 countries had raised concerns about Russia's invitation amid intensified attacks on Ukraine. Tensions have also grown after Trump waived new sanctions on Moscow and temporarily restricted logistical and intelligence support for Kyiv, further straining US-Ukraine relations",
   "bodyLevel": "fulltext",
   "country": [
    "ph",
    "ru",
    "vn",
    "eu"
   ],
   "topic": [
    "pol"
   ],
   "tier": 2,
   "actor": "美国",
