   "summary": "Korea was set to open its first Korean Cultural Center in Malaysia with a ceremony Friday. The performance hall on the first floor is equipped with a large LED panel to showcase Korean cultural content and is lined with bookshelves on both sides so visitors can use the space to read and socialize when no shows are scheduled. First Vice Minister of Culture, Sports and Tourism Kim Young-soo noted that Malaysia has a strong interest in Korean culture.",
   "summary_zh": "韩国定于星期五举行仪式，在马来西亚设立首座韩国文化中心。该中心一楼的多功能厅配有一块大型LED显示屏，用于展示韩国文化内容，厅内两侧还排列着书架，访客在没有演出安排时可在此阅读和社交。文化、体育和旅游部_first副部长金永秀表示，马来西亚对韩国文化抱有浓厚兴趣。",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "Korea was set to open its first Korean Cultural Center in Malaysia with a ceremony Friday. The new center marks the 36th such facility worldwide and the fifth in Southeast Asia. Located across from Kuala Lumpur's Petronas Twin Towers, the biggest tourist attraction in Malaysia, the venue has a 100-seat performance hall, an exhibition room, a cinema, a library and classrooms, according to Seoul's culture ministry. The performance hall on the first floor is equipped with a large LED panel to showcase Korean cultural content and is lined with bookshelves on both sides so visitors can use the space to read and socialize when no shows are scheduled. First Vice Minister of Culture, Sports and Tourism Kim Young-soo noted that Malaysia has a strong interest in Korean culture. \"We expect the center will serve as a focal point for bringing fresh momentum across the overall Korean cultural industry in cooperation with many local organizations,\" he said",
