   "snippet": "Mutaraka’ — an undeclared informal truce — appears to be the dominant strategy of the moment of the juntas in Mali and Burkina Faso vis-à-vis ISSP. ISSP’s vital expansion space lies in JNIM territory, not in government-held territories, and the most important threat to governments comes from JNIM, not ISSP. For the three Sahel juntas, JNIM is a major security and political threat, while ISSP poses a real security challenge but offers no viable or appetizing political horizon. Local juntas, their backers, and even some decision-makers could see this as a way to weaken JNIM, with the aim of tackling ISSP later. This, however, is an extremely hazardous strategy since the Sahel dynamics are moving fast and are mostly dictated by the two main warring jihadi groups @TheSoufanCenter",
